      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This article reports a case of transient augmentation of collateral circulation due to spontaneous coronary arterial spasm during angiography. The patient's electrocardiogram revealed ST-segment depression during vasospastic attack; this depression differs from the typical change of the ST-segment elevation in coronary spasm without collateral circulation."},
